    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1141">

                <pb facs="1163" n="1153" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/10–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-21T17:00:00+07:00">October 21, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 21—7:21 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 1217. Chen Tai-chu<anchor n="86" xml:id="d1141-f1"/> today admitted
                    Chinese Navy released <hi rendition="#italic">Flying Trader</hi> as well as two
                    other Isbrandtsen ships on own responsibility and that Foreign Office does not
                    yet have details. Chen previously claimed Foreign Office dictated policy on
                    detention and release (Cantel 1202, October 12).</p>
                <p>Chen felt Navy probably had insufficient vessels for continued detention these
                    ships view combat commitments. He referred with gratification to message he
                    claimed received from Chinese Embassy to effect Department advised it not
                    encouraging US flag vessels violate closure.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1141-f1" n="86" xml:id="d1141-f1-content">
                <p>Foreign Office American Department Chief.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
